 "equipment_type": "Other equipment (emergency lighting central battery system)",
 "applies_to": "CEAG DualGuard-S emergency lighting central battery systems monitored by Eaton VisionGuard software with the BACnet/IP interface licence.",
 "summary": "VisionGuard, the PC monitoring software for CEAG emergency lighting, can act as a BACnet/IP server. For each DualGuard-S system forwarded to BACnet it creates 35 status Binary Inputs, 4 battery Analog Inputs and 24 Binary Outputs for test commands, acknowledgements and 16 virtual switches.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP"
 ],
 "firmware": "VisionGuard BACnet/IP Interface V2.0",
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": true,
 "notes": [
  "From the DualGuard-S object tables (document pages 14-16). Instances here are for a system with BACnet ID 1.",
  "Instance = system BACnet ID x 1000 + consecutive object number (0-34 BI, 0-3 AI, 0-23 BO); the guide example is BACnet ID 1, BattOpenCircuit (22) = BI 1022.",
  "Object names are printed as \"X <name>\", where X is the VisionGuard BACnet ID of the system; names are kept as printed.",
  "The guide gives no access column; Binary Outputs are listed as writable, inputs as read-only. It gives no units for the battery Analog Inputs."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "VisionGuard - BACnet/IP Interface",
  "doc_number": "V2.0",
  "revision_date": "Oct. 2020",
  "url": "https://www.eaton.com/content/dam/eaton/products/safety-security-emergency-communications/emergency-lighting/central-battery-systems/vis/visionguard/en/eaton-ceag-el-cps-visionguard-bacnet-interface.pdf"
 },
 "integration": {
  "summary": "License and enable the BACnet server in VisionGuard, forward each DualGuard-S system to BACnet (it gets a BACnet ID), then read the ready, failure and mains status inputs and use the command outputs for tests and acknowledgements.",
  "minimum_points": [
   {
    "ref": "BO 1002",
    "why": "Start function test",
    "name": "X CMD_FTStart"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BO 1003",
    "why": "Start battery duration test",
    "name": "X CMD_DTStart"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BI 1000",
    "why": "Normal operation",
    "name": "X Ready"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BI 1005",
    "why": "Function test active",
    "name": "X FT"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BI 1007",
    "why": "Battery duration test active",
    "name": "X DT"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BI 1017",
    "why": "Mains failure (sum)",
    "name": "X MainsSum"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BI 1001",
    "why": "Prio 1 failure (with luminaire failure)",
    "name": "X Err1"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BI 1002",
    "why": "Prio 2 failure (without luminaire failure)",
    "name": "X Err2"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BI 1003",
    "why": "Lost communication to VisionGuard",
    "name": "X ComErrVG"
   }
  ],
  "enable": null,
  "heartbeat": null,
  "remote_sensors": null,
  "setup": [
   "VisionGuard runs the BACnet/IP server on the VisionGuard PC; it needs a licence key, and the BACnet submenu shows BACNET LICENSED and BACNET INTERFACE IN OPERATION in green when active.",
   "Server settings: device instance number, the PC network card to use and the UDP port (default 47808). BACnet Secure Connect is optional.",
   "Each forwarded system gets a BACnet ID (1-500) under Administration / BMS Forwarding."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "The objects only exist for systems forwarded to BACnet in VisionGuard; instance numbers depend on the BACnet ID given to each system.",
   "Notification classes for alarms must be created by the integrator in the BMS Forwarding / BACnet menu."
  ]
 },
